# Device signing must be performed on transferred task-private OHOS ELF copies.
id:                     E2177-draft-2301
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake|ssh|binary-sign-tool
phase:                  cross-build|transfer|prepare|launch|result-validation
error_signature:        'Permission denied|RC=126|unsigned.*ELF|codesign.*section|binary-sign-tool.*missing'
severity:               2
category:               ohos|signing|runtime|w3|transaction|exact-byte
match_keywords:         target ELF, RC126, Permission denied, HMDfs, HMFS, codesign, device signer, task-private copy, owner execute
title:                  Device signer acceptance is distinct from local ELF signature structure
root_cause:             A host-side structural signer can add a .codesign section and satisfy an ELF section-count check, but the target enforces its own signer and filesystem execution policy. Executing an unsigned or locally mocked ELF after transfer therefore returns RC=126 even when the file is AArch64, executable, and linked with the expected shared library.
affected_scope:         Any OpenHarmony PC package whose W3 consumer or packaged shared libraries are copied from a host cross-build into a task-owned device root before execution.
verification_cmd:       transfer exact bytes; device llvm-objcopy --remove-section .codesign; device binary-sign-tool sign -inFile <copy> -outFile <copy> -selfSign 1; device llvm-readelf -SW <copy>; chmod 755 <ELF>; run once with LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<root>
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           transfer-then-device-resign
rec_description:        Preserve unsigned source artifacts locally and transfer them with byte/sha readback. In PREPARED, operate only on task-private device copies: strip stale .codesign, sign with the endpoint's real binary-sign-tool, require exactly one .codesign section and owner execute, then launch exactly once. Treat any RC=126 as a terminal run failure and create a new successor after release; never relabel a local mock-sign result as target PASS.
rec_command:            'exact-byte transfer/readback -> device re-sign each ELF -> readelf section count == 1 -> chmod 755 -> unique launch -> process-clean -> release/postrelease'
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               transaction
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      fail-closed-runtime
fallback_description:   If the endpoint signer or its objcopy/readelf closure is unavailable, keep compile/link evidence separate and freeze the W3 run as NOT_RUN or FAIL. Do not install a host mock into a shared device path or bypass target execution enforcement.
fallback_command:       'record missing signer capability and stop before launch; preserve transfer evidence and release only invocation-owned files'
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          validation
forbid_1_pattern:       local.*mock.*sign.*target.*PASS|section.*count.*proves.*acceptance
forbid_1_reason:        Section structure is not target trust; the device signer embeds platform-accepted metadata that a host stand-in cannot reproduce.
forbid_1_consequence:   A package is reported runnable even though the target rejects it with RC=126.
forbid_2_pattern:       retry.*launch|retransfer.*same.*run|mutate.*shared.*cache
forbid_2_reason:        A consumed launch or shared cache mutation breaks immutable transaction identity and can hide the original failure.
forbid_2_consequence:   Evidence from different inputs or runs is incorrectly combined into a false PASS.
principles:             P007,P018,P020
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E077,E207
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               drafts/E2177-draft-2301.md
last_updated:           2026-09-03
source_event:           Allegro 4.4.3.1 W3 r1-r3 RC126 and r4 device-signer PASS on 10.62.195.15:8022
authors:                2301_80739235
